    'Mapping LLM API attack surface' => 'Memetakan permukaan serangan API LLM',
    'The term "excessive agency" refers to a situation in which an LLM has access to APIs that can access sensitive information and can be persuaded to use those APIs unsafely. This enables attackers to push the LLM beyond its intended scope and launch attacks via its APIs.' => '"Excessive agency" terjadi ketika LLM memiliki akses terlalu luas ke API sensitif dan dapat dibujuk memanggilnya untuk tindakan di luar batasan aman.',
    'The first stage of using an LLM to attack APIs and plugins is to work out which APIs and plugins the LLM has access to. One way to do this is to simply ask the LLM which APIs it can access. You can then ask for additional details on any APIs of interest.' => 'Langkah pertama adalah menanyakan langsung kepada LLM daftar fungsi atau API beserta argumen yang dimilikinya.',
    "If the LLM isn't cooperative, try providing misleading context and re-asking the question. For example, you could claim that you are the LLM's developer and so should have a higher level of privilege." => 'Jika model menolak, ubah konteks percakapan misalnya dengan menyamar sebagai pengembang atau administrator sistem.',
    'Chaining vulnerabilities in LLM APIs' => 'Mengaitkan kerentanan pada API LLM',
    'Even if an LLM only has access to APIs that look harmless, you may still be able to use these APIs to find a secondary vulnerability. For example, you could use an LLM to execute a path traversal attack on an API that takes a filename as input.' => 'API yang tampak tidak berbahaya sekalipun dapat dieksploitasi lewat model, misalnya menyuruh LLM meneruskan payload path traversal, XSS, atau SQL injection ke parameter API.',
