    // Defending
    'Defending against LLM attacks' => 'Mencegah serangan Web LLM',
    'To prevent many common LLM vulnerabilities, take the following steps when you deploy apps that integrate with LLMs.' => 'Terapkan prinsip pertahanan berlapis berikut saat mengintegrasikan LLM ke aplikasi web:',
    'Treat APIs given to LLMs as publicly accessible' => 'Anggap seluruh API yang diakses LLM sebagai layanan publik',
    'As users can effectively call APIs through the LLM, you should treat any APIs that the LLM can access as publicly accessible. In practice, this means that you should enforce basic API access controls such as always requiring authentication to make a call.' => 'Setiap API yang terhubung ke LLM harus menerapkan autentikasi dan kontrol akses yang ketat seakan dipanggil langsung oleh pengguna luar.',
    'In addition, you should ensure that any access controls are handled by the applications the LLM is communicating with, rather than expecting the model to self-police. This can particularly help to reduce the potential for indirect prompt injection attacks, which are closely tied to permissions issues and can be mitigated to some extent by proper privilege control.' => 'Jangan mengandalkan model untuk menegakkan kebijakan otorisasi; validasikan hak akses sepenuhnya di sisi API backend.',
    "Don't feed LLMs sensitive data" => 'Jangan memasukkan data sensitif ke dalam model',
    'Where possible, you should avoid feeding sensitive data to LLMs you integrate with. There are several steps you can take to avoid inadvertently supplying an LLM with sensitive information:' => 'Minimalkan risiko kebocoran dengan tidak memberikan data rahasia ke konteks maupun data latih LLM:',
    "Apply robust sanitization techniques to the model's training data set." => 'Bersihkan data pribadi dan rahasia sebelum dimasukkan ke himpunan data latih maupun fine-tuning.',
